Here is a second list of fixes for bugs and non-portable items found in myrogue clone.  Many thanks to those who reported the problems, I wouldappreciate any further reports, particularly if the stuff below doesnot fix what it is intended to fix.            Tim Stoehr            tims@zeus.TEK.COM    ---------------------------------------------------- 1.)    Change SCROLL and SCROLLS to SCROL and SCROLS respectively        throughout the code.  This is to avoid conflicts with        some curses stuff.  If your compiler doesn't complain, you        probably don't have to worry about this. 2.)    Change ALL occurences of the symbol 'UP' to 'UPWARD'.  This prevents        the definition in rogue.h from clashing with the curses definition. 3.)    There may be a nested comment around line 41 in machdep.c.        Nuke it. 4.)    In zap.c, a new version of tele_away() was sent out.  That version        needs to have the global variable 'detect_monster' added to the        list of extern booleans at the top of zap.c, if it is not already        there. 5.)    In message.c, at the bottom of the routine message(), there is code        that looks like:        if (did_int) {            onintr();        }        cant_int = 0;        It should look like the following:        cant_int = 0;        if (did_int) {            did_int = 0;            onintr();        } 6.)   In machdep.c, the routine md_slurp() shoud be changed to what is       shown below, otherwise, messages get screwed up on UNIX_BSD4_2.       Only the BSD4_2 portion needs to be changed.md_slurp(){    long ln = 0;#ifdef UNIX_BSD4_2    ioctl(0, FIONREAD, &ln);#endif#ifdef UNIX_SYSV    ioctl(0, TCFLSH, &ln);    ln = 0;#endif    ln += stdin->_cnt;    for (; ln > 0; ln--) {        (void) getchar();    }} 7.)   In monster.c, in the table m_names near the top of the file,       change "aquatar" to "aquator" and "quasit" to "quagga." 8.)   References to curses internals should be removed for the sake       of portability/compatibility.       In score.c, in the routine quit(), change these two lines:        orow = curscr->_cury;        ocol = curscr->_curx;        to:        orow = rogue.row;        ocol = rogue.col;        And in message.c, in the routine save_screen(), remove these lines        which appear at the beginning of the routine:        row = curscr->_cury;        col = curscr->_curx;        and remove these lines which appear at the bottom of the routine:        move(row, col);        refresh();        You can also them remove the local variables, row and col.